Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:34:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 186/209] feat(entity): IEntityAreaComponent::MovePoints

CArea has always had a cheap counterpart to SetPoints() - MovePoints()
(Area.cpp) updates the a2DSegments of a shape area in place when the point
count is unchanged - but it was unreachable from outside CryEntitySystem: the
only public route was IEntityAreaComponent::SetPoints(), which calls
ReleaseAreaData(), deletes and re-allocates every segment, frees the whole
per-entity containment cache and clears EAreaState::Initialized while it
rebuilds. Pushing that once per frame while a shape is dragged is allocator
churn plus a window in which the area answers no query and sends no event.

Expose it as one new virtual, appended at the END of IEntityAreaComponent
(the interface is called across DLL boundaries, so it is append-only from
here on). The component-side implementation takes local entity points exactly
as SetPoints() does, keeps m_localPoints in sync so that a later OnMove()
still has the authoritative geometry, transforms into the shared world-point
scratch buffer and calls CArea::MovePoints(). A point count that does not
match the points already set, or an area that is not a shape, is ignored -
the caller is expected to fall back to SetPoints() for those.

No behaviour change: nothing in the engine calls it yet, and the legacy
SetPoints() path is untouched.

